Title: Design a provenance-first OECD CRS and development-agency finance layer
Created: 2026-09-16
Author: Codex at author request

--- log ---
2026-09-16T00:00Z Created from the exploration of a full OECD CRS and agency-data layer.
--- body ---

## Context

The JETP pipeline now distinguishes immutable raw documents, structured
observations, best-effort reconciliation with uncertainty, and descriptive
outputs. Extend that architecture only after a bounded feasibility design for
the OECD CRS and selected OECD-country development-agency datasets. The aim is
not to claim a universal climate-finance account: CRS markers, official-flow
records, agency systems, private mobilisation and domestic finance have
different coverage and accounting semantics.

Preserve the JETP short-paper train. This is a separate data-programme design
ticket; it must not trigger a bulk download or re-scope the current paper.

## First test

Create a small CRS fixture with two releases of one activity, a Rio-marker
field, a commitment and a disbursement, plus one agency record that cannot be
linked exactly. The prototype must retain both source versions, preserve the
agency record as unresolved, and reject a combined climate-finance total across
incompatible reporting bases.

## Actions

Design and prototype a provider-adapter contract for:

1. immutable source snapshot and licence/terms metadata;
2. provider-native structured observations with mandatory free-text `notes`;
3. versioned CRS activity records, including flow type, marker semantics,
   currencies, commitments/disbursements and revision identity;
4. best-effort cross-source reconciliation with `exact`, `interval`,
   `incompatible`, `unavailable` and `unknown` outcomes; and
5. frozen descriptive views by explicitly declared accounting definition.

Map the smallest viable **prototype** wave: a bounded, documented CRS sample,
then a ranked set of JETP-relevant development-agency samples. Rank agencies
by JETP-country coverage, availability of activity-level identifiers,
revision/disbursement semantics, licence clarity and expected reconciliation
value. Specify volume, refresh cadence, raw-byte retention, DVC/partitioning,
source licensing, identifier strategy, rate-limit and reproducibility risks.
Assess whether IATI is a complement rather than an assumed complete common
denominator. Define a measurable prototype decision rule: which semantic or
linkage failures remain tolerable as explicit uncertainty, and which prevent a
future full-snapshot acquisition.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A CRS fixture proves source revisions, flow semantics and missing links survive ingestion
- [ ] Every structured observation has provenance, semantic fields and nonempty notes
- [ ] Cross-provider joins cannot silently add incompatible bases or double-count records
- [ ] The design distinguishes official reported climate-related flows from private mobilisation and domestic finance
- [ ] A phased acquisition plan names a first provider wave, storage budget and stop conditions
- [ ] Agency prioritisation is reproducible from stated coverage, identifier, semantic, licence and reconciliation criteria
- [ ] A prototype decision rule distinguishes retained uncertainty from a blocker to full-snapshot ingestion
- [ ] Licence, retention and redistribution compatibility are recorded before any real source snapshot enters storage
- [ ] A separate implementation ticket and explicit approval are required before any full-CRS or agency acquisition
- [ ] The design states whether existing DVC/object storage and snapshot contracts suffice, and names only necessary extensions

## Links

Separate programme from 0816–0827 JETP short-paper chain. Existing CRS
comparison infrastructure is relevant context, not proof that full ingestion
is ready.
